{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/138748-scion-2-0-project-enech","id":138748,"title":"Scion 2.0 Project - Enech","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-05-15T19:56:19-07:00","id":138748,"title":"Scion 2.0 Project - Enech","content":"<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\"><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/11wnXAOg0nvrWg1Vh_qOtKJRgYEUe-JKZP5RFtOQLLIc/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"font-size:48px\">Enech</span></a><br /> <br /> Hello Scion Forums! From the fine people working on the </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Scion 2.0 Project</span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">, we would like to introduce our first Pantheon Specific Purview rewrite. We decided this should be Enech because we are obsessed with all things Irish, and JSR is closing down before they got to work on their own version of Enech.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Enech is essentially life in hard mode. From the moment you chose your first geas, you are throwing yourself into the insanity that is the Tuatha\u2019s daily experience. It sets you apart from the other gods and opens you up to all the glories (and pitfalls) of Social Face. Yes, the Tuatha Gods basically embody all the gory fun of American High School politics.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Enech is powerful, but this ability comes at a steep price. When a Tuatha fails to maintain their social prowess among their fellow Irish, they soon discover that their mastery over Enech has abandoned them as they lose the confidence they need to wield their powers.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Additionally, due to the massive undertaking that our unofficial </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Scion 2.0 Project</span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\"> has become, we have begun to move all of our houserules, purview edits, knacks, birthrights, pantheons, and everything but probably the kitchen sink over to a website which we will be unveiling at the beginning of June.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">In short, this revamp of Enech serves as a teaser for what\u2019s to come, as we are excited to share our system overhaul with you. If there are any questions, we will be happy to answer them in this thread; and that includes the generalized Animal Purview, or the content of the website, or anything else Scion-related.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Enjoy!</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Aynie, Iry, and Watcher.</span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":606,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/606-aynie","user":"Aynie","date":". 05-15-2014, 10:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/606-aynie","name":"Aynie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar606_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-16T06:38:10-07:00","id":139252,"title":"","content":"Should Enech be fixed? Is that even possible? We've just replaced it completely.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-16T07:02:12-07:00","id":139273,"title":"","content":"Hush.<br /> I'm busy reading the document linked.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-16T07:58:08-07:00","id":139326,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/138748-scion-2-0-project-enech?p=139252#post139252\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Should Enech be fixed? Is that even possible? We've just replaced it completely.</div> </div> </div> </div>RAW Enech is a piece of crap. This Enech looks like a complete overhaul.<br /> Reading through it right now. Very mythical at least.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2447-twitchtherat","name":"TwitchTheRat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2447_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"134"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-16T07:58:40-07:00","id":139329,"title":"","content":"Interesting, although I fail to see how Face actually benefits you. You might get some bonuses when dealing with the T\u00faatha and the ability to use Enech Boons, but that's about it as far as I can see. With that in mind, why should it be a rank 6 Boon to get another Geas when all it does is give you is +2 maximum Face? It is a poor bonus for a Demigod, in my opinion, but maybe I just can't see it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out <a href=\"http://emeraldsamurai.com\" target=\"_blank\">Emerald Samurai</a> for my alternative character-sheets for WoD, Scion, Exalted and more.<br /> Like my <a href=\"http://www.facebook.com/EmeraldSamurai\" target=\"_blank\">Facebook page</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/308-skari-dono","name":"Skari-dono","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"104"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-16T08:02:07-07:00","id":139333,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/138748-scion-2-0-project-enech?p=139252#post139252\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Should Enech be fixed? Is that even possible? We've just replaced it completely.</div> </div> </div> </div>A glance into the linked document would reveal that while we've kept the name and the flavor of the geas and the Irish need to brag, the purview as a whole flows differently. Gone is the Irish Legend Economy (that never ran out) and we've detached geas from how RAW ran them because removing geas from the Irish is like the Greeks without their Arete.<br /> <br /> Geas now provide a social bonus towards the Irish (and only the Irish) and are the keys to unlocking and maintaining one's level of Enech (or social face). If a player breaks their geas, they're immediately barred from using the PSP until they have made amends. Later on, they can take on additional geas which in turn increases the maximum amount of &quot;Face&quot; they can build, but it's a lot more trouble than it's worth.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/606-aynie","name":"Aynie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar606_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-16T08:53:04-07:00","id":139393,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Skari-dono</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/138748-scion-2-0-project-enech?p=139329#post139329\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Interesting, although I fail to see how Face actually benefits you. You might get some bonuses when dealing with the T\u00faatha and the ability to use Enech Boons, but that's about it as far as I can see. With that in mind, why should it be a rank 6 Boon to get another Geas when all it does is give you is +2 maximum Face? It is a poor bonus for a Demigod, in my opinion, but maybe I just can't see it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Face benefits you as a representative of your social status among the Tuatha, encourages you to respect the culture of the Tuatha, serves as a gateway to keeping your PSP, and grants you additional legend with <b>Bragaire</b>.<br /> <br /> <b>Luigh Geasa</b> is a sneaky boon because many of the benefits are social. Having a geis is considered a great honor in ancient Irish culture. If you offer to lay a worthy geis upon someone who cares strongly about Irish culture, then they would lose status if they turned you down. You could even use this to manipulate the gods themselves if you could think of a geis that is worthy of a god, and if you have devious intentions then your options open up even more. You also have the choice to lay geis upon your own band members, which might be the difference between the Tuatha or their allies refusing to give that person aid or relics.<br /> <br /> From a mechanical perspective, being able to raise your maximum Face by +2 (or more if you are crazy enough to take several geis) means you can resist one more Tuatha Virtue before you start losing access to your PSP, one more satire you can endure, two more <b>Bragaire</b> you can fail, and two more points of legend every time you succeed at <b>Bragaire</b>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/484-iry","name":"Iry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar484_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"346"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-16T09:28:44-07:00","id":139417,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/138748-scion-2-0-project-enech?p=139252#post139252\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Should Enech be fixed? Is that even possible? We've just replaced it completely.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, do you have a link to yours? I would be quite interested in seeing it. I love seeing what other people have come up with.<br /> <br /> But yes, as Aynie explains, all we did was keep the name of the original Purview. Enech roughly means &quot;Honor&quot; in the context of social things, and would be equated to the idea of face in modern society. The old version of Enech has very little to do with this, but, with this new version, it encompass the entire Purview.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-16T12:42:58-07:00","id":139651,"title":"","content":"Being praised or insulted should provide a variable modifier to face, a skilled bard satireing you is worse than a cheap insult.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-16T13:18:53-07:00","id":139688,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/138748-scion-2-0-project-enech?p=139651#post139651\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Being praised or insulted should provide a variable modifier to face, a skilled bard satireing you is worse than a cheap insult.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, at the moment it is phrased as &quot;<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">someone in authority&quot;, not just anyone. The difficulty about giving it a long scaling effect depending on the societal rank, and the specific action taken to either build you up, or tear you down, is that it would become an incredibly complicate list. You would have to break down the different kinds of satires, the </span></span>Glam Dicenn, mundane insults, mundane insults dilivered in rhyme, what is the specific rank of the Bard in question, for the list is incredibly long, and so on.<br /> <br /> It is something I thought about for a while when we were designing the face system, but it was far too complicated and would require an excessive amount of book keeping on the part of the Storyteller to know what specific rank of Bard this person is, if this was a Glam Dicenn, if this was a legal situation to use the Glam Dicenn in, and so forth. So, in order to prevent things from being too complicated, we shortened it to being &quot;someone in authority&quot;.<br /> <br /> I am normally a stickler for being totally and utterly accurate, and if it was possible to do without needing a chart with about thirty different modifiers, I would totally go for it and try to work out the mechanics of it with Iry and Aynie. But, to do it any justice, it would be incredibly complicated and require excessive book keeping, something which the goal of Scion 2.0 is to reduce to allow people to run games without having to keep multiple binders full of information to reference.<br /> <br /> Now, what is important about the &quot;someone in authority&quot; tag is that it is someone who the Irish would believe is in a place of authority. So, Marduk, as a king, is in a place of authority over you as long as you are not the Ard Ri or the Chief Ollam. But, the Minister of Rivers and Floods from the Celestial Bureaucracy is not above anyone, since there is no equivalent in Irish society.<br /> <br /> I hope this makes sense as to why we do not have a large expansive system for the different kinds of insults. What I would personally suggest is for different bardic figures to take their Bard Rank as a Relic (in our system, Relics need not necessarily be something physical. If you are one of Niamh's Scions, you could take your Sidhe Blood as a Relic. Though you must always pay for it.) and give yourself a modifier to how many points of Enech you can remove or add to someone. But, it must be kept in mind that doing so illegally will have you killed. There are incredibly strict laws involving insults for the Irish.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-17T11:08:34-07:00","id":140739,"title":"","content":"So what's the point of Molfach? Like I get it's to get your deeds recognized but that mean that it's a nebulous social benefit only or does it have a mechanical benefit as well? If it's only a nebulous social benefit why not put lower in Enech and up a few of the other ones?<br /> <br /> Why is Dushlur Mor limited to reasonable requests? Maybe it's my lack of knowledge around the Irish Mythology but haven't there been times when unreasonable requests have been forced upon someone? I get that it's a balance issue but it seems like something that wouldn't be an issue.<br /> <br /> Finally, Morgacht, Maybe it's because I remember Me but isn't 2 Legend kind of weak for Purviews but strong for Knacks. The bonus seems a bit disproportionate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-17T12:23:36-07:00","id":140814,"title":"","content":"Looks interesting. My group will have to give it a try and see how the Tuatha and the storyteller like it.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/138748-scion-2-0-project-enech?p=140739#post140739\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So what's the point of Molfach? Like I get it's to get your deeds recognized but that mean that it's a nebulous social benefit only or does it have a mechanical benefit as well? If it's only a nebulous social benefit why not put lower in Enech and up a few of the other ones?</div> </div> </div> </div>I cannot speak for any of the others, but my guess it has the same benefit as things like rumor mill and trendsetter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1505-charles-red","name":"Charles Red","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-17T13:05:07-07:00","id":140826,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/138748-scion-2-0-project-enech?p=140739#post140739\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So what's the point of Molfach? Like I get it's to get your deeds recognized but that mean that it's a nebulous social benefit only or does it have a mechanical benefit as well? If it's only a nebulous social benefit why not put lower in Enech and up a few of the other ones?</div> </div> </div> </div>There is no strict mechanical benefit to having Molfach, but not every power should be strictly mechanical. One of the great difficulties as a Scion is that you are going to be meeting people who have no idea who you are, for you are a minor little <i>thing</i>, not even entirely Divine. And on top of that, you're probably also a foreigner, meaning that Gods, Goddesses, and Legendary Beings from other Pantheons are probably going to have no idea who you are, or care.<br /> <br /> What Molfach lets you do is <i>force</i> those people to know who you are. If you tricked Isis into telling you her true name, the true name of Horus, and the true name of Osiris through a cunning plan, you could have used this power to make sure everyone knows just what you did. If you manage to disarm Thor, and shave his beard while grappling him to shame him, coming away from it unharmed, you can have even the Deva know what you did. It gives you a tremendous amount of Social power, both making sure that others know just who you are, how amazing you are, and being able to use it to shame others by their horrible defeats at your hands.<br /> <br /> Now, the reason it is not lower is because every Boon before it fits incredibly well into the Rank they have been slotted into. The order of things has been highly considered, and everything fits nicely into the slot it has been given both mechanically and mythically. The order of Boons is to attempt to build up a Scion and their player into taking the Irish mentality of taking great risks, and having both great rewards, but also failures. The Boons before this allow the Scion to build themselves up to the point where they can take these great risks with the ability for great reward, but also failure. So, the placement of Molcach at Rank 5 is to continue building on that theme, before moving into the more Divine aspects of Enech.<br /> <br /> Does the value of the Boon make sense to you with that explained Epimetheus? I can try to further explain if it does not.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/138748-scion-2-0-project-enech?p=140739#post140739\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why is Dushlur Mor limited to reasonable requests? Maybe it's my lack of knowledge around the Irish Mythology but haven't there been times when unreasonable requests have been forced upon someone? I get that it's a balance issue but it seems like something that wouldn't be an issue.</div> </div> </div> </div>All powers have to be designed to prevent people from intentionally breaking the game, people will abuse the rules if they can. This prevents someone from defeating Ra when he is Avatared down in a contest and forcing him to blink, thus ending all of reality.<br /> <br /> But, to explain it from a mythological point of view, yes, requests had to be sensable. If you asked someone to bring you the moon, everyone would agree that you were being a twat for doing so. People would lose respect for you. But, if you were cunning about it, as Lugh was with the three brothers who killed his father, he made an entirely reasonable request, &quot;Gather these items for me,&quot;, but managed to twist it around so that the items they had to gather tired them out and wore them down so they could be killed by the final tasks, you would be honored.<br /> <br /> Irish mentality is quite difficult to grasp in the modern day, but just assume if you are being direct, and exerting your power over someone else in a way which is cruel, or mean, even if you have a right to, people will look down on you, and you will be shamed. But, if you manage to be cunning about it, trick them, make a safe situation suddenly become a cruel or mean one, that's totally fine and you will be praised for it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/138748-scion-2-0-project-enech?p=140739#post140739\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Finally, Morgacht, Maybe it's because I remember Me but isn't 2 Legend kind of weak for Purviews but strong for Knacks. The bonus seems a bit disproportionate.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am really sorry, but this bit I'm having a bit of a problem following. Which Me Boon are you talking about? I couldn't see anything similar to this concept, reducing the cost of something when I checked.<br /> <br /> And, while RAW there is defiantly a disparage between the costs of Knacks and Boons, and in the amount of power each wield, we are rewriting every single Purview, and every single Epic Attribute. Legend costs are going to be balanced out so that there will not be this disparage of power between the two.<br /> <br /> I hope that answers your questions Epimetheus, please let me know if it doesn't or if you have any more. I am happy to help explain our choices.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charles Red</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/138748-scion-2-0-project-enech?p=140814#post140814\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Looks interesting. My group will have to give it a try and see how the Tuatha and the storyteller like it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wicked, I'm glad you guys are going to check it out. If you get any questions or concerns, be sure to poke us.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","user":"Watcher","date":". 05-17-2014, 04:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-20T15:34:44-07:00","id":143917,"title":"","content":"Awesome!!! My main character was a Tuatha, so this rewrite of Enech is just... amazing, truly honey on the lips.<br /> <br /> I have a question, though. That Ultimate Power, <b>Bua</b>, feels awesome as written. Is a really great concept, that &quot;Break the Limit&quot; (and everything else!). But mechanically is a little bit weak, in my honest opinion. I mean, after an EPIC battle, in which you are burning Legend, when comes the most decisive moment, that perfect instant... you probably don't have much Legend points to spend, and anyway the <i>One Legend Point = One Success</i> ratio doesnt' feel really Ultimate. <br /> <br /> Of course i'm taking into consideration the old system in which your Epic Attributes were above the clouds, showing the character with tons of successes. Maybe the mechanics are different in this new Scion and therefore i don't have a good perspective on this. ^^<br /> <br /> Thank you anyway for this little piece of Scion 2.0!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Userhat Aegpts Vlrs. </span><span style=\"color:#996633\">Coren &quot;Ojos de Fuego&quot;. </span><span style=\"color:#666699\">Mithrael. </span><span style=\"color:#ffcc00\">Menehet.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1349-phersus","name":"Phersus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1349_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-20T20:11:01-07:00","id":144039,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Phersus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/138748-scion-2-0-project-enech?p=143917#post143917\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Awesome!!! My main character was a Tuatha, so this rewrite of Enech is just... amazing, truly honey on the lips.</div> </div> </div> </div>Awesome, I'm very glad you like it and you will get a chance to use it. Let us know what you think of it after giving it a go.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Phersus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/138748-scion-2-0-project-enech?p=143917#post143917\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have a question, though. That Ultimate Power, <b>Bua</b>, feels awesome as written. Is a really great concept, that &quot;Break the Limit&quot; (and everything else!). But mechanically is a little bit weak, in my honest opinion. I mean, after an EPIC battle, in which you are burning Legend, when comes the most decisive moment, that perfect instant... you probably don't have much Legend points to spend, and anyway the <i>One Legend Point = One Success</i> ratio doesnt' feel really Ultimate.<br /> <br /> Of course i'm taking into consideration the old system in which your Epic Attributes were above the clouds, showing the character with tons of successes. Maybe the mechanics are different in this new Scion and therefore i don't have a good perspective on this. ^^</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, no worries. I'm glad you are asking questions, though I am not the perfect person to answer them. Iry is our mechanics person, I just produce ideas and work on our site. But, I will do my best.<br /> <br /> To set the stage mechanically, we still use the Epic Attribute Autosuccess scale, so as a Legend 11 God, you will have 46 Autosuccesses at base to work with. We have, however, slashed many of the ways to gain passive bonus dice, or Autosuccesses to things. Birthrights may not give additional Automatic Successes, or Dice, to give an example. We have also slashed most of the Boons which can give you bonus Dice and Autosuccesses, though each Purview has at least one, though it is minor to be sure. Virtues, at God, can give you Automatic Successes, and so can Legendary Deeds, though they are quite limited.<br /> <br /> But, onto the topic of Bua itself.<br /> <br /> Bua is actually not designed to be used at just the perfect moment after you have fought through the opposing army to reach its general to strike them down. You, of course, can use it for this function, but it would not be quite as powerful as possible, for you are worn down by that point. Bua is designed to encourage you to be horribly, horribly reckless, to do something amazing, but stupid. As is, actually, the vast majority of Enech. We want Irish Scions to be encourage to take colossal gambles, take massive risks, and have the potential for both awe inspiring success, and bitter loss.<br /> <br /> So, to encourage that theme, Bua is most effective when you go all in on a single thing. You put every ounce of yourself into making a single play, and you will be better at it than anyone else could ever have been (unless they used an Avatar or Ultimate, but I will get to that in a moment). And, while you will Succeed, if you played your cards wrong, if this victory did not win you the war, you are now horribly weakened with zero Legend remaining, and you will have to make it through the entirety of the Story, desperately Stunting, doing more and more reckless things to regenerate your Legend. (No just going to the Teotl and asking for Legend. We are already giving Itztli some looks and poking at it.)<br /> <br /> Furthermore, Bua is incredibly versatile. A Legend 11 Bard, without a Dot of Epic Strength, could pick up a stone and throw it through the eye of Surtr, just as Lugh did with Balor long before. Horribly maiming the Fire Giant, without a doubt, if they use it when they have a large amount of Legend left. A Warrior could sit down and discover the way to save Lir's children, and bring the ancient Titan back into the fold of the Pantheon, likely throwing Midir under the bus to do so, but hey, he's stupid. A blind man could find Airmed's herbs, and bring Miach back to life with them. But, all of these things will leave the young God who did them, if they threw every ounce of themselves at the problem, quite weakened, So, you must chose very wisely.<br /> <br /> Additionally, on the topic of Ultimates and Avatars. A Scion who uses Bua will never be as good as a fellow Deity in one of these states. A God using Ultimate Strength will be stronger, a Goddess using The General will be better. But, what this power does is fly under the Mutually Assured Destruction bar that Ultimates and Avatars carry. When one being uses an Avatar, or an Ultimate, everyone else jumps into one too, to ensure some safety to themselves, or to combat the immediate threat in the only way possible. If you use The General to challenge Bres to single combat, Bres smacks you over the head with Ultimate Appearance. If you use Ultimate Charisma to win a peace between the Yazata and Deva, Shiva pops The Void as his role as The Destroyer, and then Vishnu pops The Sentinel, and it just becomes a mess.<br /> <br /> Bua, not being one of the Ultimates or Avatars, however, does not cause this immediate panic from all the other Deities. You have the ability to effectively acomplish a goal uncontested, unless it is something someone is willing to blow an Avatar or Ultimate over and start a chain reaction, with the only issue being that you are going to be horribly weakened for the rest of the Story. You have to take a horrible risk to be utterly amazing, and that's what being Irish is all about. Bad choices and being awesome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-04T11:56:54-07:00","id":159252,"title":"","content":"Ok! Sorry for the delay (damm you, real life) Anyway, here i am again, with news and reports about the Tuatha! <br /> <br /> As i was pretty excited with the new and fresh rework of <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"color:#008000\"><u><b>Enech</b></u></span></span>, i conviced our ST to run for us a brief Scion session in Nuada's court this weekend. Long story short, the plot was Dagda's uprising against Nuada in a critical moment: a reunion between the Aesir and the Irish Gods. The reason behind the encounter was the extermination of the alliance between the Fomorians and the Northern Giants. Morrigan had forseen the destruction of the Tuatha's King in the following battle, and so Dagda tried to dethrone Nuada, in order to assume himself the King's death.<br /> <br /> Anyway. The players picked both Tuatha's and Aesir Gods (all of them formerly Scions, having reached Apotheosis in the last Chronicle) to play. Without further delay, these are our impressions:<br /> <br /> <b><u>Great things:</u></b><br /> <br /> -The new feeling of Enech. The Tuatha have now that Irish vibrant feeling. The new Enech contributes to the feeling of playing with characters larger than life, boisterous and passionate. It's much, much more energetic now (old Enech always felt somewhat oppresive if you get my meaning: sometimes it felt like it was more punishment than anything else) and, well, organic: the system of Face is really dynamic. <br /> <br /> -Right now Enech improves the social intercourse in a scene, and through the use of some Boons (specially <b>D\u00fashl\u00e1n M\u00f3r (</b>\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 \u2022\u2022<b>)</b>, we loved that one so much) the story developes by itself, something we really appreciate. It eases pressure for the ST when it's needed. Great tool.<br /> <br /> -I'm going to say it again: <b>D\u00fashl\u00e1n M\u00f3r</b>: awesome. Whoever thought of it, you have our love. Take it.<br /> <br /> <br /> <u><b>Doubts:</b></u><br /> <br /> - <b>Feabhas (\u2022\u2022):</b> Can you use it in conjunction with 10, in order to magnify even more that last power?<br /> <br /> - <b>Altram (\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022):</b> Feels more like a Merit than a Enech Boon. Maybe it could be better to link it to the transition to Demigod directly, sort of a xp-free, special Tuatha bonus? <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <u><b>Details that could use a little love:</b></u> <br /> <br /> - Maybe make some graduation between Geas. You can have anything as a Gea, so it would be nice if harder Geas had better rewards.<br /> <br /> - We missed one power that directly taped into Fate itself, as Irish have this powerful conection to Fate. I'll write more on that later. <br /> <br /> - <b>Luigh Geasa</b> <b>(</b>\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 \u2022<b>)</b>: Players that get Geas but don't obtain Face benefits tend to feel it as a punishment or limitation, rather than something to help them evolve their characters concepts. One suggestion here: <br /> <br /> - Maybe you could consider to give them a benefit (albeit a marginal one), apart from the special social bonus with Tuatha. Maybe the Geas this power creates could help to recover Legend, for instance, to Tuatha and foreigners alike. Thus, it would help to mitigate the heavy cost of <b>Bua</b> <b>(</b>\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022<b>)</b>, something we really feel necessary.<br /> <br /> - <b>M\u00f3rgatch</b> <b>(</b>\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022<b>)</b>: The specialization concept about this Boon was original and greatly appreciated. (One of the players, in fact, suggested that this could be done to all the Gods, or at least possess some Knack or Bonn so inherently tied to each God nature that, once reached Apotheosis, could become free). If you are familiar with Mage the Awakening, could be something similar to Attainements. In fact, if that power (whoever it would be, it surely should have some limitations like don't take a powerful and offensive boon, like in MtA.) Alternatively, you could discount as much Legend as the Legend Rating of the God. If the cost reach zero, that's it. <br /> <br /> <br /> - <b>Bua</b> <b>(</b>\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022<b>)</b>: Powerful and impressive. Once played like your opening gambit is in fact awesome. But there's a problem with it. Using it feels... unworthed. Alas, you can perform ONE impressive action... at the price of being unable to do anything later. That forced supression feels anticlimatic. Moreso, if things get twisted and everybody starts tapping into Avatar.... oh, you're fucked. No Legend, no Avatar. No Avatar... well. Oh and one doubt: please clarify that &quot;<i>such an action is written into Fate&quot;</i>. Has some mechanical benefit to that? If not, maybe it should. We missed some Enech directly messing with Fate.<br /> <br /> - Our suggestion regarding Bua? Create some form of rapidly harvesting Legend if the action feels right enough, maybe via Luigh Geasa. <br /> <br /> Anyway, great work. Congrats, team, and thank you for the closeness and the involvement with us fans!<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Userhat Aegpts Vlrs. </span><span style=\"color:#996633\">Coren &quot;Ojos de Fuego&quot;. </span><span style=\"color:#666699\">Mithrael. </span><span style=\"color:#ffcc00\">Menehet.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1349-phersus","name":"Phersus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1349_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-04T12:57:26-07:00","id":159294,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Phersus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/138748-scion-2-0-project-enech?p=159252#post159252\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">-The new feeling of Enech. The Tuatha have now that Irish vibrant feeling. The new Enech contributes to the feeling of playing with characters larger than life, boisterous and passionate. It's much, much more energetic now (old Enech always felt somewhat oppresive if you get my meaning: sometimes it felt like it was more punishment than anything else) and, well, organic: the system of Face is really dynamic.</div> </div> </div> </div>Awesome, I am glad you guys enjoyed it and tried it out. I will do my best to adress your concerns, but I am sure Iry will show up later to explain his reasoning behind the mechanics.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Phersus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/138748-scion-2-0-project-enech?p=159252#post159252\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">- <b>Feabhas (\u2022\u2022):</b> Can you use it in conjunction with 10, in order to magnify even more that last power?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, entirely. If you would like to do so, there is nothing stopping you. As a Legend 12 God, if you blow a Deed, a Rank 5 Virtue, and Bua (full pool), you could drop 179 Successes on something.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Phersus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/138748-scion-2-0-project-enech?p=159252#post159252\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">- <b>Altram (\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022):</b> Feels more like a Merit than a Enech Boon. Maybe it could be better to link it to the transition to Demigod directly, sort of a xp-free, special Tuatha bonus?</div> </div> </div> </div>Altram is supposed to have that sort of a feel, but it is incredibly closely tied with the concept of Face. You have to prove yourself before someone is willing to leave their child under your tutelage (just in case anyone doesn't know, the Foster system would be more like an Apprentice system in the modern era, you are not really 'part of the family', but more so are being trained or training someone else) or take you on. It is a lot of social responsibility all tied up in that power.<br /> <br /> But, what do you mean by making it into a &quot;xp-free, special Tuatha bonus&quot;? I'm just having a hard time following what you mean. If you mean that every Tuatha, at Demigod, just 'gets' this sort of thing for no cost, that would be fairly unbalanced, though I don't think that's what you mean, just what I am getting from the sentence. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Phersus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/138748-scion-2-0-project-enech?p=159252#post159252\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">- Maybe make some graduation between Geas. You can have anything as a Gea, so it would be nice if harder Geas had better rewards.</div> </div> </div> </div>Every Geas should be roughly equally difficult for a Scion, maybe we will write that into the rules somewhere, it may not be as obvious as it should be. But, the Storytellers should be seeing to this as their role as Fate. One person who must leave a mark on every land they visit, and someone who has to follow all the rules of hospitality at all times, both should have an equally difficult time. Those who have 'easy' Geasa shouldn't be given an easy time. Fate should see to that.<br /> <br /> But, I totally get that that's not obvious, and we will put that in somewhere. I feel silly for overlooking that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Phersus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/138748-scion-2-0-project-enech?p=159252#post159252\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">- <b>Luigh Geasa</b> <b>(</b>\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 \u2022<b>)</b>: Players that get Geas but don't obtain Face benefits tend to feel it as a punishment or limitation, rather than something to help them evolve their characters concepts. One suggestion here:<br /> <br /> - Maybe you could consider to give them a benefit (albeit a marginal one), apart from the special social bonus with Tuatha. Maybe the Geas this power creates could help to recover Legend, for instance, to Tuatha and foreigners alike. Thus, it would help to mitigate the heavy cost of <b>Bua</b> <b>(</b>\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022<b>)</b>, something we really feel necessary.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't really understand the basis of this, I'm sorry. I'll try to explain what's going on, and if I'm totally missing the point, swoop in and correct me. If a Player doesn't want a Geas, they can't receive one. Only a willing party can take a Geas, it can't be used as a punishment, or a curse. Therefore, it should always be something to help them evolve their character concepts, or to play into a character concept.<br /> <br /> Additionally, every additional Geas one person gains through Luigh Geasa increases your possible Face pool, so, it should always be giving Face benefits. I don't believe there is a way to do so with it doesn't give any.<br /> <br /> Giving the Geas any mechanical benefit asides from the (intentionally) minor buff to social interactions with the Tuatha violates the concept of a Geas. In modern terms, it is playing a game in such a way that you are imposing limitations on yourself to make your life harder. Such as playing through a game without getting any unnecessary kills, playing through an entire co-op game alone and on the hardest difficulty, those sorts of things, just so you can say you did.<br /> <br /> Upon giving a Geas a mechanical benefit, such as increasing Legend regain, it ruins it as a Geas. A Geas is something which has no up side except that you can show the world how awesome you are, for look at what great deeds you accomplished while at the same time imposing great limitations on yourself.<br /> <br /> Also, we are trying to get away from Legend regaining stuff in Scion 2.0. We are going to take a knife to Itztli, and you will only be regaining Legend back from sacrifices at God to better fit in line with the Aztec cosmology, since only the Gods receive the power from sacrifices. (Griffinguy will be helping us with it) We will still encourage sacrifices through other ways (the Scion regains Virtue channels, gains 'favor' with a God [not sure how we will do that one], supercharges their Willpower, and so on), but you won't be getting Legend back until Legend 9.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Phersus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/138748-scion-2-0-project-enech?p=159252#post159252\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">- <b>M\u00f3rgatch</b> <b>(</b>\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022<b>)</b>: The specialization concept about this Boon was original and greatly appreciated. (One of the players, in fact, suggested that this could be done to all the Gods, or at least possess some Knack or Bonn so inherently tied to each God nature that, once reached Apotheosis, could become free). If you are familiar with Mage the Awakening, could be something similar to Attainements. In fact, if that power (whoever it would be, it surely should have some limitations like don't take a powerful and offensive boon, like in MtA.) Alternatively, you could discount as much Legend as the Legend Rating of the God. If the cost reach zero, that's it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Unfortunatly, I am totally unfamiliar with Mage, but I believe Iry knows it well, he can probably better answer this than I can, so I'm going to leave this one to him. It also deals with mechanics of balance and cost reductions, so it is far more up his alley than mine. I'm just about the accuracy of things.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Phersus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/138748-scion-2-0-project-enech?p=159252#post159252\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">- <b>Bua</b> <b>(</b>\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022<b>)</b>: Powerful and impressive. Once played like your opening gambit is in fact awesome. But there's a problem with it. Using it feels... unworthed. Alas, you can perform ONE impressive action... at the price of being unable to do anything later. That forced supression feels anticlimatic. Moreso, if things get twisted and everybody starts tapping into Avatar.... oh, you're fucked. No Legend, no Avatar. No Avatar... well. Oh and one doubt: please clarify that &quot;<i>such an action is written into Fate&quot;</i>. Has some mechanical benefit to that? If not, maybe it should.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, okay, I see what's going wrong here. We run Avatars and Ultimates very much as a Last Resort of the Gods because it instantly starts an arms race and Gods are /going/ to die in that Scene as soon as someone pops one. Unless it is in an entirely friendly situation where an Avatar, for some reason, is needed. <br /> <br /> So, with that in mind, Bua is designed to let the Irish skirt that line. They can do something insane, and not instantly start everyone kicking off into their Avatars and Ultimates. It lets an Irish God just decide they are going to win without knowing that they just broke the Mutually Assured Destruction line.<br /> <br /> If someone runs Avatars and Ultimates as something the Gods use very often, the power of Bua becomes very 'meh', but, that's not the way we run it at all. Iry, once again, can do a better job of explaining here.<br /> <br /> But, the &quot;such an action is written into Fate&quot; line has zero rules based mechanical benefit. What that means is if a character uses Bua, whatever they did just became super, duper important. If they just did it on something totally irrelevant for some reason, the Storyteller should shift things around to change that. If you use Bua to accomplish something you are normally entirely unskilled with (keep in mind, if I have Epic Appearance 2, I can still use Bua on my Appearance and blow people away with it), you're probably going to be Fatebound to that concept now.<br /> <br /> It is intentionally left free form since every single use of Bua can't be accounted for, we can't really make it flatly mechanical, and we have to trust the Storytellers to make things epic and awesome without giving them a step by step instruction guide to do so since all uses of Bua could be so incredibly different and amazing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Phersus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/138748-scion-2-0-project-enech?p=159252#post159252\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We missed some Enech directly messing with Fate.</div> </div> </div> </div>Unfortunately, all of the things with old Enech where it was tied to Fate and so on are entirely fictional and non-accurate. The Irish didn't believe that one's Enech had anything at all to do with their Fate. Sometimes people had Fates that involved their Geasa, but they didn't commonly go hand in hand.<br /> <br /> So, in order to continue our strive for accuracy, Enech has no real 'Fate' based power asides from Bua. I am very sorry if some people are upset by that, but if you really wanted, you could do something with a Relic Unique Power to model some of the old interactions of Enech and Fate if you would like. But, as the base Purview, the idea of Enech (social standing) is miles and miles away from the idea of Fate.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Phersus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/138748-scion-2-0-project-enech?p=159252#post159252\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anyway, great work. Congrats, team, and thank you for the closeness and the involvement with us fans!</div> </div> </div> </div>I am really glad you guys liked it as much as you did. If you use it any more, and have any other conclusions drawn, please be sure to poke us. And, if I misunderstood anything, please just let me know.<br /> <br /> Oh, and also, were you using Scion 2.0's rules for this game? Or were you just using RAW / Houseruled RAW? Just curious.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-05T14:39:43-07:00","id":160284,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Watcher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/138748-scion-2-0-project-enech?p=159294#post159294\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But, what do you mean by making it into a &quot;xp-free, special Tuatha bonus&quot;? I'm just having a hard time following what you mean. If you mean that every Tuatha, at Demigod, just 'gets' this sort of thing for no cost, that would be fairly unbalanced, though I don't think that's what you mean, just what I am getting from the sentence.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, actually i meant that. (By the way, excuse me if at some point i don't speak properly. English is not my native language) I didn't thought it was unbalanced because of the special effort you have to put on sustaining the relationship: could be something you get for free, but it definitely won't be easy or comfortable to maintain, you'll have to work hard on it. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Watcher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/138748-scion-2-0-project-enech?p=159294#post159294\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Every Geas should be roughly equally difficult for a Scion, maybe we will write that into the rules somewhere, it may not be as obvious as it should be. But, the Storytellers should be seeing to this as their role as Fate. One person who must leave a mark on every land they visit, and someone who has to follow all the rules of hospitality at all times, both should have an equally difficult time. Those who have 'easy' Geasa shouldn't be given an easy time. Fate should see to that.<br /> <br /> But, I totally get that that's not obvious, and we will put that in somewhere. I feel silly for overlooking that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Don't feel silly! Is a HUGE work the one you're doing. We're here to help you guys! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> (yes, i'm a fanboy of Scion xD)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Watcher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/138748-scion-2-0-project-enech?p=159294#post159294\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't really understand the basis of this, I'm sorry. I'll try to explain what's going on, and if I'm totally missing the point, swoop in and correct me. If a Player doesn't want a Geas, they can't receive one. Only a willing party can take a Geas, it can't be used as a punishment, or a curse. Therefore, it should always be something to help them evolve their character concepts, or to play into a character concept.<br /> <br /> Additionally, every additional Geas one person gains through Luigh Geasa increases your possible Face pool, so, it should always be giving Face benefits. I don't believe there is a way to do so with it doesn't give any.</div> </div> </div> </div>I understand the point of it, but still is... hard. Yes, i know that's the point of having Geas, but at least Tuatha enjoy some benefits derived from them (namely, the use of Enech). The outsider gets zero incentive to keep his/her Face high. Mmmm how about a mechanical bonus to social intercourse with the Tuatha? Sort of the thing you imply in the description, but mechanically defined, like a &quot;bonus equal to your actual Face in your social dice rolls concerning the Tuatha&quot;. If the Gea was related to violence could apply only to Intimidation rolls, while if was along the concept of diplomacy or just manners could help in Empaty, or something like that.<br /> <br /> As i'm writing this i'm thinking on one of your sentences <i>&quot;Upon giving a Geas a mechanical benefit, such as increasing Legend regain, it ruins it as a Geas. A Geas is something which has no up side except that you can show the world how awesome you are, for look at what great deeds you accomplished while at the same time imposing great limitations on yourself.&quot; </i>and as i get what you mean, i'm starting to have doubts about the proposed bonus. But... well, just give it a thought, and then tell me.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Watcher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/138748-scion-2-0-project-enech?p=159294#post159294\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Unfortunatly, I am totally unfamiliar with Mage, but I believe Iry knows it well, he can probably better answer this than I can, so I'm going to leave this one to him. It also deals with mechanics of balance and cost reductions, so it is far more up his alley than mine. I'm just about the accuracy of things.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair enough! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Watcher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/138748-scion-2-0-project-enech?p=159294#post159294\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ah, okay, I see what's going wrong here. We run Avatars and Ultimates very much as a Last Resort of the Gods because it instantly starts an arms race and Gods are /going/ to die in that Scene as soon as someone pops one. Unless it is in an entirely friendly situation where an Avatar, for some reason, is needed.<br /> <br /> So, with that in mind, Bua is designed to let the Irish skirt that line. They can do something insane, and not instantly start everyone kicking off into their Avatars and Ultimates. It lets an Irish God just decide they are going to win without knowing that they just broke the Mutually Assured Destruction line.<br /> <br /> If someone runs Avatars and Ultimates as something the Gods use very often, the power of Bua becomes very 'meh', but, that's not the way we run it at all. Iry, once again, can do a better job of explaining here.<br /> <br /> But, the &quot;such an action is written into Fate&quot; line has zero rules based mechanical benefit. What that means is if a character uses Bua, whatever they did just became super, duper important. If they just did it on something totally irrelevant for some reason, the Storyteller should shift things around to change that.<b> If you use Bua to accomplish something you are normally entirely unskilled with (keep in mind, if I have Epic Appearance 2, I can still use Bua on my Appearance and blow people away with it), you're probably going to be Fatebound to that concept now.</b><br /> <br /> It is intentionally left free form since every single use of Bua can't be accounted for, we can't really make it flatly mechanical, and we have to trust the Storytellers to make things epic and awesome without giving them a step by step instruction guide to do so since all uses of Bua could be so incredibly different and amazing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you for the detailed explanation. I actually love that highlighted part, about being Fatebound. I think you should include that in the description, at the very least as an idea. It's a great one. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Watcher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/138748-scion-2-0-project-enech?p=159294#post159294\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Unfortunately, all of the things with old Enech where it was tied to Fate and so on are entirely fictional and non-accurate. The Irish didn't believe that one's Enech had anything at all to do with their Fate. Sometimes people had Fates that involved their Geasa, but they didn't commonly go hand in hand.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh? Ok, my ignorance is speaking here, but i genuinelly thought Enech was tied to Fate. Cu Chulainn and Morrigan, and all that. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Watcher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/138748-scion-2-0-project-enech?p=159294#post159294\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, in order to continue our strive for accuracy, Enech has no real 'Fate' based power asides from Bua. I am very sorry if some people are upset by that, but if you really wanted, you could do something with a Relic Unique Power to model some of the old interactions of Enech and Fate if you would like.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, it was nothing like upset, but that idea about the Relic is a cool one. Thank you! I'll bring it to them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Watcher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/138748-scion-2-0-project-enech?p=159294#post159294\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, and also, were you using Scion 2.0's rules for this game? Or were you just using RAW / Houseruled RAW? Just curious.</div> </div> </div> </div>Houseruled RAW, we hadn't read the new rules of the web yet. By the way, there's something i wanted to ask you all. Did you considered making Willpower another Epic Attribute? I ask because in the old game the resistance to Epic Manipulation was a problem. And all the powers mind-bending also! <br /> <br /> Thank you for your attention!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Userhat Aegpts Vlrs. </span><span style=\"color:#996633\">Coren &quot;Ojos de Fuego&quot;. </span><span style=\"color:#666699\">Mithrael. </span><span style=\"color:#ffcc00\">Menehet.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1349-phersus","name":"Phersus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1349_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-05T15:16:21-07:00","id":160307,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Phersus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/138748-scion-2-0-project-enech?p=160284#post160284\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, actually I meant that. (By the way, excuse me if at some point i don't speak properly. English is not my native language) I didn't thought it was unbalanced because of the special effort you have to put on sustaining the relationship: could be something you get for free, but it definitely won't be easy or comfortable to maintain, you'll have to work hard on it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah mate, no worries, you are just perfect at it. If there are any misunderstandings, it will probably be from my end.<br /> <br /> But, running the Foster Retainer or Guide like that is totally possible, but, for Guides, it's actually the standard way we run it. A Guide can, and will, ask favors of you. And, additionally, if you do something to bug them enough, you will suddenly lose them as a Guide as they cease to mentor you. It is different for Retainers, but also possible if they are individually thinking enough. Though, a Retainer is less likely to ask you a favor.<br /> <br /> For example, Charles, a young fiery Theoi has his wife Zoe as his Guide. Normally, he doesn't bother to resist his Vengeance as part of the way I represent his connection to Fire, but when his wife is around, she will whisper in his ear and calm him down so that I will actually roll, and pay the willpower to fight off the Virtue. If Charles continually ignored her, their relationship would turn horribly sower, especially since that is the way the previous 'versions' of their Relationship have gone and Fate loves a pattern. (Gaia and Ouranos, Rhea and Cronus, Hera and Zeus) So, in our base system, a Retainer and a Guide are already a two way street.<br /> <br /> But, if you don't run it that way, and have it so people are bound by Fate to be your Guide or Retainer, giving it to the Irish for free with that extra strenuious benefit could be alright, but it would probably have to be kept a close eye on the first few times it is done just to watch the balance of it.<br /> <br /> Oh, and, sometimes your Guide can hate you and want to kill you but still function as your Guide, it's explained on our Guide page. But, in that case, if your 'Nemesis' Guide suddenly stopped antagonizing you, you would lose them as a Guide since you are no longer constantly being tested by them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Phersus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/138748-scion-2-0-project-enech?p=160284#post160284\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I understand the point of it, but still is... hard. Yes, i know that's the point of having Geas, but at least Tuatha enjoy some benefits derived from them (namely, the use of Enech). The outsider gets zero incentive to keep his/her Face high. Mmmm how about a mechanical bonus to social intercourse with the Tuatha? Sort of the thing you imply in the description, but mechanically defined, like a &quot;bonus equal to your actual Face in your social dice rolls concerning the Tuatha&quot;. If the Gea was related to violence could apply only to Intimidation rolls, while if was along the concept of diplomacy or just manners could help in Empaty, or something like that.<br /> <br /> As i'm writing this i'm thinking on one of your sentences <i>&quot;Upon giving a Geas a mechanical benefit, such as increasing Legend regain, it ruins it as a Geas. A Geas is something which has no up side except that you can show the world how awesome you are, for look at what great deeds you accomplished while at the same time imposing great limitations on yourself.&quot; </i>and as i get what you mean, i'm starting to have doubts about the proposed bonus. But... well, just give it a thought, and then tell me.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, outsiders have no reason at all to keep their Geasa, but it is slightly intentional. I believe they are intended, however, to receive the social benefit, so I will bring that up with Iry. It would probably just be a flat bonus, without any specific things such as being only for intimidation, but they should still get something. The social benefit is actually something that we debated heavily on, and as time goes on, I am slightly more and more unsure of it. It was designed to represent the prestige you get from having one, rather being a function of the Geas itself, but if it is not coming off like that, maybe we will reword it.<br /> <br /> I know it is really hard for us, in the modern era, to really grasp the concept of a Geas, and even want to take one for one of our characters, since they are literally nothing but a hasle for you. But, they were incredibly important for the Irish. I understand if some people have a hard time grasping the essence of them, it is a concept that has grown incredibly foreign to us. Making one's life intentionally exceptionally harder just to say you did.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Phersus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/138748-scion-2-0-project-enech?p=160284#post160284\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thank you for the detailed explanation. I actually love that highlighted part, about being Fatebound. I think you should include that in the description, at the very least as an idea. It's a great one.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, we may have to. I am just unsure of it since there are so many possible ways to represent the 'Fate takes notice' part of Bua. If you used it to seduce someone, and Fate was particularly cruel that day, they may have it turn into a Medea-esque situation. There are many hundreds of ways it could be represented, and I am afraid if we put a direct mechanical possibility, that will be the road most often taken.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Phersus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/138748-scion-2-0-project-enech?p=160284#post160284\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh? Ok, my ignorance is speaking here, but i genuinelly thought Enech was tied to Fate. Cu Chulainn and Morrigan, and all that.</div> </div> </div> </div>No worries, I can really understand the confusion. Old Enech made it seem that way, but they are very separate ideas that tend to collide only when there needs to be a tragedy. This is because of how dear the Irish held one's Social standing, so, therefore, having one's Geasa be the cause of one's doom was deeply cutting in the Irish mentality. So, it's not so much as them being connected, but the Geas being an easy medium to the idea of social standing, and causing the cruel Fate to be even more heart wrenchingly tragic.<br /> <br /> But, The Morrigan and the CuChulain situation was actually because of the prophecy that CuChulain bound himself to. CuChulain allowed himself have the prophecy of being the greatest warrior in Ireland, but to be doomed to die young (Very much like the Achilles Prophecy). So, in order for that to come true, CuChulain refused The Morrigan, who took it unto herself to ruin his shit. Leading to CuChulain killing his lover/foster brother, breaking his Geasa, and eventually dying. In the process, he showed the world that he was the greatest warrior in Ireland, but his death was separate form his Face for all facts but he broke his Geasa to further make his death a tragedy.<br /> <br /> The idea that if you break a Geas you will just die soon is a inconsistent one unfortunately. Sometimes people seem to have that looming over their head, and sometimes they don't. Some people break Geas and die, and some don't. So, in order to make it playable, we went with it just not spelling your immediate doom.<br /> <br /> What was likely the root of this idea of it spelling your doom is that if you broke a Geas, you would likely have been socially ostracized, and thrown out of your tribe/kingdom/ect, which is something that would spell your doom since in a Bronze Age wilderness, you really need a society to support you if you want to survive.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Phersus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/138748-scion-2-0-project-enech?p=160284#post160284\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, it was nothing like upset, but that idea about the Relic is a cool one. Thank you! I'll bring it to them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Glad to help. If you need any suggestions for what the Relic could be, just poke me. I'm more than happy to help with the Tuatha.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Phersus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/138748-scion-2-0-project-enech?p=160284#post160284\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Houseruled RAW, we hadn't read the new rules of the web yet. By the way, there's something i wanted to ask you all. Did you considered making Willpower another Epic Attribute? I ask because in the old game the resistance to Epic Manipulation was a problem. And all the powers mind-bending also!</div> </div> </div> </div>We did not make Willpower an Epic Attribute, but we did make a way to resist Social Powers. At base, it is bound to either one's Epic Wits, or their Epic Intelligence, but Knacks can be taken to apply one's Epic Charisma, or Epic Appearance (by making targets either not want to sway your thoughts, or strike them with that horrible awkwardness teenagers have when they are trying to talk to someone horribly attractive) to their Mental Defense Value (MDV) of beings who are sentient. (You can't use your Appearance to help you resist a drug that effects your mind, for example. But you could use your Intelligence)<br /> <br /> Just let us know if you have any other questions, we are very glad you have enjoyed it as much as you have.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","user":"Watcher","date":". 06-06-2014, 02:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-11T14:36:31-07:00","id":1127786,"title":"","content":"Watcher, I have recently read some information on the Brehon Laws and in particular the status of daughters. How does being a daughter of a Tuatha de Danann factor into Enech? It seems to be there would be some difference in the amount of face one could hold. And also would they inherit any property if the reached the God tier? If I remember correctly daughters could inherit Movable property. This is troubling to me and makes me unsure of using this purview, so I have been looking for other alternatives, even though honour was according to records a huge part of ancient Irish society. Am I right to be concerned? And lastly if I am right in being concerned about this, then how can faery queens claim lands (such as Muster) as theirs?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13647-manannansun","name":"Manannansun","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"78"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-18T20:00:00-07:00","id":1131095,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Manannansun</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/138748-scion-2-0-project-enech?p=1127786#post1127786\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Watcher, I have recently read some information on the Brehon Laws and in particular the status of daughters. How does being a daughter of a Tuatha de Danann factor into Enech? It seems to be there would be some difference in the amount of face one could hold. And also would they inherit any property if the reached the God tier? If I remember correctly daughters could inherit Movable property. This is troubling to me and makes me unsure of using this purview, so I have been looking for other alternatives, even though honour was according to records a huge part of ancient Irish society. Am I right to be concerned? And lastly if I am right in being concerned about this, then how can faery queens claim lands (such as Muster) as theirs?</div> </div> </div> </div>Alrighty! Sorry about the delay, I had a bit of a medical problem but now I'm back on my feet able to ramble about this stuff.<br /> <br /> Okay, so. The status of women in pre-Christian Ireland is really complicated, as we don't strictly have anything purely from the period itself. Sort of the problem we always have. The Brehon Laws are one of the more trusted sources, but even they are not recorded until after the Christianization process has already been more-or-less finished. We do know that the Celts were not a Super Feminist, Peace-Loving, Nature-Worshiping, Classless Society as was the popular image of them circa the 1970-80s, but women had it fairly well? I mean, being a woman in the ancient world generally sucked, but Ireland wasn't the worst place. Upper-Class men did practice Polygamy, but it's kinda unclear exactly to what degree this was since the chieftians/kings were entering into sexual-religious relationships with local Tutelary Deities which means they are probably sitting at at least two wives each. Except one of them is, well, a Deity and probably isn't really around the place. One of the base units of wealth, the <i>Cumal</i> is a female slave, three of which is worth one cow, which doesn't speak particularly highly of the status of women.<br /> <br /> However, at the same time of all of this, women seem to be doing some pretty awesome, radical stuff, <i>especially</i> in the literature. Queen Medb is a queen in her own right, using her sexuality to get her way. She is independently powerful from her husband, and wields so much influence she brings all of Ireland to war with Ulster, and emerges victorious against CuChulain even when he has The Morrigu (or, well, 2/3 of The Morrigus. Nemean and Badb are on CuChulain's side helping him in the battles, but The Morrigan ends up working against him) and Lugh on his side. (Technically, while she <i>does</i> win, the magical bull she wanted ends up getting killed like instantly after making the whole war pointless) She is a badass, powerhouse of a figure. She obviously has a huge amount of personal honor, wielding it with horrific capability. She shames others into helping, uses her own position as a political tool, is fiercely independent, everything.<br /> <br /> At the same time, however, Medb can be seen to have direct control of her daughter's body. Medb uses her daughter Findabair's body as a tool to get other people to do what she wants. She destroys Findabair's own personal agency in the face of her own political goals, constantly offering up Findabair's body and promising to marry her to one person or another to get people to make the suicidal feat of trying to kill CuChulain. <br /> <br /> Other instances of women with massive amounts of personal honor / Enech would be Macha, Emer, and Scathach. Macha's personal honor is why she ends up cursing the Ulstermen. She is <i>challenged</i>, her husband accidentally drops the fact that she can run faster than horses, and the King demands to see this. Macha, despite being nine months pregnant, can't just say 'no'. Sure, the king would kill her husband for big-talk if she didn't run, but that isn't why she runs. She does it because she is challenged, her honor is on the line. And, when her honor is then insulted by having to give birth in the mud before of all of the Ulstermen, none of which try to help I will point out, she levies a curse on them. The story of Macha is a story of Enech, her upholding her personal honor, and unleashing a massively powerful war-curse upon an entire kingdom when that honor is insulted.<br /> <br /> Emer is slightly different. She is the best of woman, the peak, the height, the paragon of being a woman. (You will notice, being 'The Best' is a very common theme in Irish literature) In the story of <i>Bricriu's Feast</i>, we see Enech playing the main role. The trickster Bricriu manages to bring Ulster to its knees through manipulating the greatest heroes of Ulster into fighting each other over who is the greatest. He does the same with the greatest women of Ulster, the wives of these three champions, each of whom viciously argues and verbally spars with each other over which of them is greatest. Emer emerges victorious here, and she is considered without a doubt the greatest woman of Ireland. When Fand tries to carry CuChulain away, it is Emer rolling up with fifty of her handmaidens all armed to the teeth with knives that scares the shit out of both CuChulain and Fand. And after some degree of threatening, Fand leaves with Manannan saying that Emer and CuChulain deserve only each other as they are the perfect man and woman respectively. Even when Emer and CuChulain are, like, eight years old (because keep in mind, The Morrigan tries to jump CuChulain's bones when he's like... 12? 11? <i>Really</i> young, young enough he's not considered a man, and thus not targeted by the curse) Emer tests CuChulain, the pair of them speaking to each other in riddles, flirting with each other in a way that none of Emer's handmaidens / wardens know what they are talking about. I would argue that Emer is just as Honor-dependent as CuChulain is, the pair of them perfect for each other as they are the paragons of their sexes. (And Emer being the 'paragon' shows you a lot of what a high-status woman would be able to acomplish, at least from a literary perspective, which is <i>a lot</i>. Like, shaming kings, shaming Gods, threatening a Fairy Queen with a knife if she doens't step off her husband)<br /> <br /> And then Scathach has Enech in a way that may be more familiar, she is a martial paragon. She is the greatest trainer of heroes, and has high standards for her apprentices. CuChulain is the Best Hero, so he has to be trained by the Best Trainer. That best trainer happens to be a woman, and the text doesn't really make any point of this past the sexual angle that goes on. Scathach has an enormous amount of Enech, her personal honor so high that she is The Best, and by being trained by her, CuChulain can be The Best. If he hadn't been trained by her, that would be a mark against his honor. So, I would argue that Scathach has a massive amount of personal honor, she is certainly swimming in Enech. She's not even a local, she's got so much honor that some kid in central-Northern Ireland knows that he has to travel to Scotland, through the Shadowlands (poorly explained past the name) to reach her. Her reputation travels far.<br /> <br /> So, that is why I would argue that women are just as legitimate users of Enech as men. There might be slightly different standards of what being Excellent means if one wants to be a paragon of their sex, but if you want to be a paragon of a profession, your sex won't matter. <br /> <br /> ----<br /> <br /> Okay, now for the second question! Could a woman Scion of the Tuatha inherit things as a Deity. Sure, absolutely. The Tuatha might not actually obey the Brehon Laws, those were brought by The Sons of Mil. I don't know if there are any references to any of the Tuatha being Brehons. And, even if they are, people don't follow the rules all the time. If you are rich and powerful, you can do what you want. If you just became Ri, the normal task at hand is to kill all of your male siblings, and uncles, and nephews. Unless you like them, in which case just blind them or otherwise main them. The Brehon Laws don't want people doing that, but it was not uncommon, a good way to cement your power.<br /> <br /> So, if, for example, Lugh had a daughter who entered... whoever your Storyteller is running as the current Ri of the Pantheon's hall, and gained a position in the tribal society, Lugh could totally give her whatever he wanted on his (second) death. She might need to fight for it since inheritance fights are normal, or Lugh might need to make it public knowledge that he wants her to inherit XYZ, but it would be fine. If you are big, powerful, and influential, you can ignore the rules more or less.<br /> <br /> Women inheriting land was not super common, but we do have two examples I know of form literature. Medb, as discussed above, is granted an entire Kingdom to herself by... her father I believe. Her father or husband, but I think father. And then there is another example of a woman becoming a Ri... oh, what's her name. Macha Mong-ruiad, yeah. She rules as Ri for a while at one point after her father dies, and waging successful war against those who disagreed with her. So, for a Scion, it should be no difficulty at all.<br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> And for the last bit, some Fairy Queens are claimed to have some ownership of land most likely because they were probably not always Fairy Queens. They were probably originally local Tutelary Deities, local Soverignty figures for the regional chieftians, that sort of thing. So they owned the land just like Macha owned Ulster, or Eriu and her sisters owned Ireland as a whole, kinda-sorta-sorta-kinda.<br /> <br /> I hope all of this answers your question though! I think it's totally appropriate for a woman to use Enech, just as much as a man. But, if you are still uncomfortable with it, I can try to help you brainstorm a new PsP for the Tuatha if you'd like.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}